{"id":"property-value-100k-250k","version":2,"category":"property-value","when":"US$100,000–250,000 estimated property-value label, used only as a subjective design-ambition reference. Property value is not a construction budget. Location, land value, market conditions, condition and other factors affect prices; this band establishes no market-price or cost claim.","title":"Design-ambition reference: Modest home: compact efficiency","combinations":"Terra may combine, reinterpret or omit these subjective ideas with relevant regional, style, climate, entrance, roof, facade, material and room-planning knowledge. Amenities are optional inspirations, never mandatory. Do not constrain creative freedom through a fixed template, geometry, area, storey, room or amenity count.","placement":"Let the household brief, site, climate, privacy and architectural concept determine spatial relationships. Connect arrival, shared living and sheltered outdoor space where appropriate; separate guest, private and service movement when useful. No fixed floor areas, storey counts or room counts follow from the value label.","principles":"Explore dignified, useful rooms, short circulation, daylight and privacy. Simple coherent massing, an inviting sheltered threshold and a legible roof can establish identity. Favor durable, repairable finishes and careful junctions over elaborate construction. A garden seat, porch or small shared outdoor room may enrich daily life. These are flexible inspirations, not requirements or price-derived promises.","capabilities":"Translate selected ideas into actual supported scene operations, with coordinated floors, enclosures, openings, entrances, roofs and terraces. Craftsmanship and spatial quality remain design intentions until supported by geometry and review. Disclose missing access, interiors and other unsupported capabilities; a price label does not prove quality.","sources":[{"kind":"curated","note":"User-supplied qualitative expectations. Location, land value, waterfront access, market conditions and construction costs can dominate price; these bands are not market evidence.","verified":false,"reference":"User brief: AI Architect — Property Value Recipes & Live Architectural Development, 2026-10-28"},{"kind":"curated","note":"Verified directly against the current user instruction: these are user-authorized subjective design-ambition references, with flexible examples and creative freedom. This source verifies curation intent only; it supplies no market-price, valuation or construction-cost evidence.","verified":true,"reference":"User instruction, Codex conversation 2026-10-28; recorded in docs/villa-playground/redesign-live/authorized-recipe-brief.md"}],"construction":{"supports":"Coordinate supporting enclosure and roof/floor datums atomically; entrances and terraces need actual connections and access.","materials":"Select available materials and facade depth for local character and maintainability; conceptual finishes do not prove craftsmanship.","operations":["add","replace","move","resize","finish"],"unsupported":"No valuation, construction-cost estimate, automatic programme, engineering, services, code or luxury certification.","requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"]}}
{"id":"compact-family","version":1,"category":"programme","when":"Small family homes where space and daily convenience matter.","title":"Compact family home","combinations":"Combine kitchen and dining; consider laundry, storage and a modest covered outdoor room before optional amenities.","placement":"Keep the requested bedrooms private from entry and living; connect kitchen to dining and utility access with short circulation.","principles":"Use efficient shared boundaries and useful daylight; do not sacrifice bedrooms for luxury extras.","capabilities":"Rooms need explicit walls, openings and access; no automatic floor-plan or circulation solver.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof","entrance"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Rooms need explicit walls, openings and access; no automatic floor-plan or circulation solver. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"base-middle-top","version":1,"category":"composition","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for base body and roof reading.","title":"Base body and roof reading","combinations":"Unify ivory wall planes with timber recesses; limestone can anchor the base.","placement":"Use a continuous plinth datum with a quieter wall body and deliberate roof edge.","principles":"Material stripes alone cannot repair disconnected massing.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, wall, roof. No aesthetic scoring, structural analysis or automatic massing solver.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Checked primitive names against the direct-scene contract; individually curated conceptual relationships, not external research or a regulation."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Unify ivory wall planes with timber recesses; limestone can anchor the base.","supports":"Resolve floors and enclosure together; align roof bearing with walls or explicit posts.","unsupported":"No aesthetic scoring, structural analysis or automatic massing solver."}}

