{"id":"french-court-residence","version":1,"category":"tradition","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for french inspired arrival court.","title":"French inspired arrival court","combinations":"Choose compatible ivory limestone timber or bronze from the scene palette; names do not imply specialist finishes.","placement":"Frame a formal approach with a principal residence and lower service edges.","principles":"Do not invent mansard geometry beyond supported roof forms.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, wall, roof, entrance. No arbitrary arches, carved orders, decorative meshes or exact historical reconstruction.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Checked primitive names against the direct-scene contract; individually curated conceptual relationships, not external research or a regulation."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof","entrance"],"materials":"Choose compatible ivory limestone timber or bronze from the scene palette; names do not imply specialist finishes.","supports":"Express character through actual enclosure, openings, eaves and occupied exterior spaces.","unsupported":"No arbitrary arches, carved orders, decorative meshes or exact historical reconstruction."}}
